import Mathlib
import MassGap.ClusterRoute

/-!
# MassGap.GenerationCyclic — the generation clause as cyclicity of the observer's vectors

`ClusterRoute.NarrowInputsAtCL` carries the generation clause beyond the margin,
`∀ P, BeyondR r P → ApproxKAt (kernC … 0) (mixKG hN2 W … r) (gramF hN2 W r) P`. In the joint Hilbert space
`ApproxJoint.JH` of composites and observer it is a statement about two closed real subspaces: `obsV`, the
closed real span of the observer's margin vectors, and `allV`, the closed real span of all joint vectors
(composites and observer). This module states the clause as `ObserverCyclic : allV ≤ obsV` (a restatement of the
generation clause, `cyclic_iff_forall`, `narrowAtCL_iff_cyclic`, not a discharge), proves the equivalence,
proves `obsV_iterate` (the observer's vectors at any later margin span `obsV`, the analogue, argued in §4, of
the time half of Reeh–Schlieder; no theorem here consumes it, and `ObserverCyclic` remains the open input in
full), and proves the linear core of the smoothing-inversion route. Declarations are in the namespace `MassGap.GenerationCyclic`.

## 1. Density lemmas (any real normed or inner product space)

* `mem_of_closure_span`: a continuous linear map sending a set into a closed subspace sends the closed span
  of the set there.
* `map_closure_le`: `A (closure K) ⊆ closure (A K)`.
* **`le_of_denseRange`**: if `A` has dense range on `L = closure span S` (relative to `L`) and sends `S`
  into a closed subspace `V`, then `L ≤ V`.
* **`closure_map_eq_of_symm`**: in a complete real inner product space, a symmetric continuous linear map,
  injective on a closed subspace `L` and mapping `L` into itself, has dense range in `L`: the part of `L`
  orthogonal to `A L` is killed by `A` (`⟪Az, Az⟫ = ⟪z, A(Az)⟫ = 0`).
* **`closure_span_image_eq`**: for such `A` with `A S ⊆ closure span S`, `closure span (A S) = closure span S`.
* **`le_of_symm_injective`**: for such `A` sending `S` into a closed `V ≤ closure span S`,
  `closure span S = V`. This is the linear form of smoothing inversion: an injective symmetric smoothing
  (no contraction bound is used) loses nothing in closed span, so smoothed fields are dense among fields.

## 2. The joint space

For `D : ApproxJoint.JointData I M`:

* `obsV D`, `allV D` (closed real spans in `JH D`), `obsV_le_allV`, `isClosed_obsV`, `obsV_coe`.
* `mem_obsV_iff`: `ApproxKAt P ↔ jv (inl P) ∈ obsV` (`ApproxJoint.approxKAt_iff_mem`).
* **`ObserverCyclic D`**: `allV D ≤ obsV D`, i.e. `obsV D = allV D`: the observer's margin vectors are
  cyclic, for the real closed span, in the subspace generated by all joint vectors.
* **`cyclic_iff_forall`**: `ObserverCyclic D ↔ ∀ P, ApproxKAt P` (that is, `ApproxK`).
* **`cyclic_iff_beyond`**: for any predicate `B` reached from every composite by some step iterate,
  `ObserverCyclic D ↔ ∀ P, B P → ApproxKAt P` (`ApproxJoint.approxKAt_of_iterate`).
* `stepR`, `stepR_symm`: the step as a real symmetric map.
* **`obsV_iterate`**: for every `m n`, the closed real span of the observer's vectors moved `n` steps of
  size `a_m` later is `obsV D`. The step is symmetric and injective (`ApproxJoint.step_injective`), so
  `closure_span_image_eq` applies at each step.
* `Smoothing D`: a real-linear continuous `A` on `JH D`, symmetric, injective on `allV D`, carrying every
  joint vector into `obsV D`. **`cyclic_of_smoothing`**, `cyclic_of_denseRange`, and
  **`smoothing_iff_cyclic`** (`A = id` for the converse).

## 3. The generation clause

* `ObserverCyclicCL hN2 W hphys z μ`: `ObserverCyclic` of `ApproxJoint.capData` at `CRen N z μ`, for some
  `ClassMoments` and `CompOS` witnesses.
* **`generation_of_cyclic`**: `ObserverCyclicCL → ` the generation clause beyond `r` (no other input).
* **`cyclic_of_generation`**: under `SubstrateCoreCL`, `ExpandStrong`, `ClusterPM`, `CovC`, `CompNondeg`,
  `PhysRange r`, the generation clause gives `ObserverCyclicCL` (`exists_beyond_iterate`).
* `NarrowCyclicAtCL`: `NarrowInputsAtCL` with the generation clause replaced by `ObserverCyclicCL`.
  **`narrowAtCL_iff_cyclic`**: the two bundles are equivalent. Both carry `RunSeedN.EndpointN N`, refuted by
  `EndpointAudit.not_endpointN_of_levels_unbounded` under the argued growth of the zero-flux level count, so no
  `ClayStatement` capstone is stated from them; the generation clause is the same in
  `ClayRunSeed.NarrowInputsAtRS`.

## 4. Reading (argued; no declaration)

Reeh–Schlieder. The Reeh–Schlieder theorem has two halves: the vacuum is cyclic for the algebra of all
fields (by construction of the theory from its fields), and analyticity of time translation carries
cyclicity from all times to any open time interval. Here an analogue of the second half is proved in
Euclidean form, for the later half-line of margins (any later margin), not for a bounded interval:
`ApproxJoint.step_injective` (every step injective, from every monomial being a step of a monomial) gives
the margin reduction `approxKAt_of_shift` and `obsV_iterate` (the observer's vectors at any later margin
span `obsV`). Injectivity of the transfer plays the role analyticity plays in the Minkowski proof.
`ObserverCyclic` is the first half for the observer's field algebra inside the joint space: the composites
are not observer fields by definition (they carry `a_k^{−d}` and their own subtractions, while `Φ0 W`
scales only the plaquette class), so it is a statement, not a construction. `ApproxObserver.
exists_jointRPK_not_approxK` and `ProxyGenLimN.decoupled_core` show it does not follow from the kernels
with joint positivity.

Smoothing inversion. `GenerationN` §0: the observer reads every local gauge-invariant field `O` as
`O ∘ V_k^W` (factor `a_k⁻⁴` on the plaquette class), so each joint vector would lie in `obsV` if the
`W`-flowed reading of a field were the image of its unflowed vector under one operator `A` on `JH`.
`le_of_symm_injective` then needs only symmetry of `A` and injectivity on `allV`. In a free (Gaussian)
theory with linear flow `φ_s = e^{sΔ} φ`, the flowed Wick monomials are `Γ(e^{s₀Δ})` applied to the
unflowed ones, and `Γ(e^{s₀Δ})` is a positive, injective, symmetric contraction: smoothed fields are dense
among fields, and the clause would hold in that case for the Wick-ordered fields. `smoothing_iff_cyclic` shows
that `Smoothing D` is not weaker than `ObserverCyclic D` (take `A = id`): the smoothing route moves the
content into the identification of one `A` for which `A (jv x) ∈ obsV` is read from the flow.

The interacting gap, stated precisely: there is no operator on `JH` built here whose action on the vector
of a composite monomial is the vector of the same monomial with every field replaced by its `W`-flowed
reading. `O ↦ O ∘ V_k^W` is linear on functions of the lattice configuration, but `V_k^W` is a nonlinear
map of configurations; the composition operator is neither symmetric for the reflection form `rform
(stateK k)`, nor bounded uniformly in `k`, nor compatible with the `a_k^{−d}` renormalisation of the
composites. The remaining input is therefore `ObserverCyclicCL` itself, or a `Smoothing` operator for
`capData`: a symmetric operator on the joint space, injective on `allV`, carrying every composite vector
into the observer's closed span.

Foundational footprint only (`#print axioms` at the end).

DERIVED (module-wide): `0` the zero vector, the plane, the reference step and the zero iterate; `1` the
successor step; `2` the least colour count.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

noncomputable section

namespace MassGap.GenerationCyclic

open Filter
open scoped Topology

/-! ## 1. Density lemmas -/

section Normed

variable {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [NormedSpace ℝ H]

/-- **A continuous linear map sending a set into a closed subspace sends its closed span there.**
DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem mem_of_closure_span {S : Set H} {A : H →L[ℝ] H} {V : Submodule ℝ H}
    (hV : IsClosed (V : Set H)) (h : ∀ x ∈ S, A x ∈ V) :
    ∀ x ∈ (Submodule.span ℝ S).topologicalClosure, A x ∈ V := by
  have hle : (Submodule.span ℝ S).topologicalClosure ≤ V.comap (A : H →ₗ[ℝ] H) := by
    refine Submodule.topologicalClosure_minimal _ ?_ ?_
    · rw [Submodule.span_le]
      exact fun x hx => h x hx
    · exact hV.preimage A.continuous
  exact fun x hx => hle hx

/-- **The image of a closure lies in the closure of the image.** DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem map_closure_le (A : H →L[ℝ] H) (K : Submodule ℝ H) :
    K.topologicalClosure.map (A : H →ₗ[ℝ] H) ≤ (K.map (A : H →ₗ[ℝ] H)).topologicalClosure := by
  rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  have hx' : x ∈ closure (K : Set H) := by
    rw [← Submodule.topologicalClosure_coe]
    exact hx
  have hmaps : Set.MapsTo A (K : Set H) (K.map (A : H →ₗ[ℝ] H) : Set H) :=
    fun y hy => ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
  have := map_mem_closure A.continuous hx' hmaps
  rw [← Submodule.topologicalClosure_coe] at this
  exact this

/-- **Dense range on the closed span carries the closed span into any closed subspace that holds the
images.** If `L = closure span S` lies in the closure of `A L` and `A S ⊆ V` with `V` closed, then
`L ≤ V`. DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem le_of_denseRange {S : Set H} {V : Submodule ℝ H} (hV : IsClosed (V : Set H))
    (A : H →L[ℝ] H)
    (hd : (Submodule.span ℝ S).topologicalClosure
      ≤ ((Submodule.span ℝ S).topologicalClosure.map (A : H →ₗ[ℝ] H)).topologicalClosure)
    (hAS : ∀ x ∈ S, A x ∈ V) : (Submodule.span ℝ S).topologicalClosure ≤ V := by
  refine hd.trans (Submodule.topologicalClosure_minimal _ ?_ hV)
  rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  exact mem_of_closure_span hV hAS x hx

end Normed

section Inner

variable {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H] [CompleteSpace H]

/-- **A symmetric map injective on a closed invariant subspace has dense range there.** With
`K = closure (A L)` and `x = y + z`, `y ∈ K`, `z ∈ Kᗮ`: `z ∈ L`, `A (A z) ∈ K`, so
`⟪A z, A z⟫ = ⟪z, A (A z)⟫ = 0`, `A z = 0`, `z = 0`. DERIVED: `0` the zero vector. -/
theorem closure_map_eq_of_symm {L : Submodule ℝ H} (hL : IsClosed (L : Set H)) (A : H →L[ℝ] H)
    (hA : ∀ x y, inner ℝ (A x) y = inner ℝ x (A y)) (hinj : ∀ x ∈ L, A x = 0 → x = 0)
    (hAL : ∀ x ∈ L, A x ∈ L) : (L.map (A : H →ₗ[ℝ] H)).topologicalClosure = L := by
  set K := (L.map (A : H →ₗ[ℝ] H)).topologicalClosure with hKdef
  have hKL : K ≤ L := by
    refine Submodule.topologicalClosure_minimal _ ?_ hL
    rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    exact hAL x hx
  refine le_antisymm hKL fun x hx => ?_
  haveI : CompleteSpace K := (Submodule.isClosed_topologicalClosure _).completeSpace_coe
  obtain ⟨y, hy, z, hz, rfl⟩ := K.exists_add_mem_mem_orthogonal x
  have hzL : z ∈ L := by
    have e : z = (y + z) - y := (add_sub_cancel_left y z).symm
    rw [e]
    exact L.sub_mem hx (hKL hy)
  have hm : A (A z) ∈ K := Submodule.le_topologicalClosure _ ⟨A z, hAL z hzL, rfl⟩
  have h1 : inner ℝ z (A (A z)) = 0 := Submodule.inner_left_of_mem_orthogonal hm hz
  have h2 : inner ℝ (A z) (A z) = 0 := by
    rw [hA]
    exact h1
  have hz0 : z = 0 := hinj z hzL (inner_self_eq_zero.mp h2)
  rw [hz0, add_zero]
  exact hy

/-- **Symmetric injective smoothing keeps the closed span**: if `A` is symmetric, injective on
`closure span S` and `A S ⊆ closure span S`, then `closure span (A S) = closure span S`.
DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem closure_span_image_eq {S : Set H} (A : H →L[ℝ] H)
    (hA : ∀ x y, inner ℝ (A x) y = inner ℝ x (A y))
    (hinj : ∀ x ∈ (Submodule.span ℝ S).topologicalClosure, A x = 0 → x = 0)
    (hAS : ∀ x ∈ S, A x ∈ (Submodule.span ℝ S).topologicalClosure) :
    (Submodule.span ℝ (A '' S)).topologicalClosure = (Submodule.span ℝ S).topologicalClosure := by
  set L := (Submodule.span ℝ S).topologicalClosure with hLdef
  have hL : IsClosed (L : Set H) := Submodule.isClosed_topologicalClosure _
  have hAL : ∀ x ∈ L, A x ∈ L := mem_of_closure_span hL hAS
  have hspan : Submodule.span ℝ (A '' S) = (Submodule.span ℝ S).map (A : H →ₗ[ℝ] H) :=
    (Submodule.map_span (A : H →ₗ[ℝ] H) S).symm
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · refine Submodule.topologicalClosure_minimal _ ?_ hL
    rw [Submodule.span_le]
    rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    exact hAL x (Submodule.le_topologicalClosure _ (Submodule.subset_span hx))
  · rw [hspan]
    calc L ≤ (L.map (A : H →ₗ[ℝ] H)).topologicalClosure := (closure_map_eq_of_symm hL A hA hinj hAL).ge
      _ ≤ _ := Submodule.topologicalClosure_minimal _ (map_closure_le A _)
          (Submodule.isClosed_topologicalClosure _)

/-- **Smoothing inversion, linear form**: a symmetric map, injective on `closure span S`, sending `S`
into a closed `V ≤ closure span S`, forces `closure span S ≤ V`. DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem le_of_symm_injective {S : Set H} {V : Submodule ℝ H} (hV : IsClosed (V : Set H))
    (hVL : V ≤ (Submodule.span ℝ S).topologicalClosure) (A : H →L[ℝ] H)
    (hA : ∀ x y, inner ℝ (A x) y = inner ℝ x (A y))
    (hinj : ∀ x ∈ (Submodule.span ℝ S).topologicalClosure, A x = 0 → x = 0)
    (hAS : ∀ x ∈ S, A x ∈ V) : (Submodule.span ℝ S).topologicalClosure ≤ V := by
  rw [← closure_span_image_eq A hA hinj fun x hx => hVL (hAS x hx)]
  refine Submodule.topologicalClosure_minimal _ ?_ hV
  rw [Submodule.span_le]
  rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  exact hAS x hx

end Inner

/-! ## 2. The joint space -/

section Joint

open MassGap.CompositeLink MassGap.ApproxJoint

variable {I M : Type} (D : JointData I M)

/-- **The observer's closed real span** in the joint space. DERIVED: no numeral. -/
def obsV : Submodule ℝ (JH D) :=
  (Submodule.span ℝ (Set.range fun Q : M => jv D (Sum.inr Q))).topologicalClosure

/-- **The closed real span of all joint vectors.** DERIVED: no numeral. -/
def allV : Submodule ℝ (JH D) :=
  (Submodule.span ℝ (Set.range (jv D))).topologicalClosure

/-- **The observer's margin vectors are cyclic in the joint space**: `allV D ≤ obsV D`.
DERIVED: no numeral. -/
def ObserverCyclic : Prop := allV D ≤ obsV D

/-- DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem isClosed_obsV : IsClosed (obsV D : Set (JH D)) := Submodule.isClosed_topologicalClosure _

/-- DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem obsV_le_allV : obsV D ≤ allV D :=
  Submodule.topologicalClosure_mono (Submodule.span_mono (by
    rintro _ ⟨Q, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨Sum.inr Q, rfl⟩))

/-- `obsV` is the closure of the real combinations `yL`. DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem obsV_coe :
    (obsV D : Set (JH D)) = closure (Set.range (yL fun Q : M => jv D (Sum.inr Q))) := by
  have hspan : ((Submodule.span ℝ (Set.range fun Q : M => jv D (Sum.inr Q))
      : Submodule ℝ (JH D)) : Set (JH D)) = Set.range (yL fun Q : M => jv D (Sum.inr Q)) := by
    ext y
    rw [SetLike.mem_coe, Finsupp.mem_span_range_iff_exists_finsupp]
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨c, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨c, rfl⟩
    · rintro ⟨c, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨c, rfl⟩
  rw [obsV, Submodule.topologicalClosure_coe, hspan]

/-- **`ApproxKAt` is membership in `obsV`.** DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem mem_obsV_iff (P : I) : ApproxKAt D.Kc D.X D.G P ↔ jv D (Sum.inl P) ∈ obsV D := by
  rw [approxKAt_iff_mem, ← SetLike.mem_coe, obsV_coe]

/-- **Cyclicity is `ApproxK`**: every composite is approximated iff the observer's vectors are cyclic.
DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem cyclic_iff_forall : ObserverCyclic D ↔ ∀ P : I, ApproxKAt D.Kc D.X D.G P := by
  constructor
  · intro h P
    rw [mem_obsV_iff]
    exact h (Submodule.le_topologicalClosure _ (Submodule.subset_span ⟨Sum.inl P, rfl⟩))
  · intro h
    show (Submodule.span ℝ (Set.range (jv D))).topologicalClosure ≤ obsV D
    refine Submodule.topologicalClosure_minimal _ ?_ (isClosed_obsV D)
    rw [Submodule.span_le]
    rintro _ ⟨x | x, rfl⟩
    · exact (mem_obsV_iff D x).1 (h x)
    · exact Submodule.le_topologicalClosure _ (Submodule.subset_span ⟨x, rfl⟩)

/-- **Cyclicity is the clause on any set of composites reached by step iterates**
(`approxKAt_of_iterate`). DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem cyclic_iff_beyond (B : I → Prop) (hB : ∀ P, ∃ m n : ℕ, B ((D.shI m)^[n] P)) :
    ObserverCyclic D ↔ ∀ P, B P → ApproxKAt D.Kc D.X D.G P := by
  rw [cyclic_iff_forall]
  refine ⟨fun h P _ => h P, fun h P => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨m, n, hn⟩ := hB P
  exact approxKAt_of_iterate D m n P (h _ hn)

/-- The step as a real continuous linear map. DERIVED: no numeral. -/
def stepR (m : ℕ) : JH D →L[ℝ] JH D := (step D m).restrictScalars ℝ

/-- DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem stepR_symm (m : ℕ) (x y : JH D) :
    RCLike.re (inner ℂ (stepR D m x) y) = RCLike.re (inner ℂ x (stepR D m y)) := by
  show RCLike.re (inner ℂ (step D m x) y) = RCLike.re (inner ℂ x (step D m y))
  rw [step_symm]

/-- **The observer's span at later margins** (the analogue of the time half of Reeh–Schlieder; not consumed
here): the observer's vectors moved `n` steps of size `a_m` later have
closed real span `obsV D`. Each step is symmetric and injective (`step_injective`) and maps the
observer's vectors to observer vectors (`step_jv`); `closure_span_image_eq`. DERIVED: `0` the zero
iterate; `1` the successor step. -/
theorem obsV_iterate (m n : ℕ) :
    (Submodule.span ℝ (Set.range fun Q : M => jv D (Sum.inr ((D.shM m)^[n] Q)))).topologicalClosure
      = obsV D := by
  letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ (JH D) := InnerProductSpace.complexToReal
  induction n with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ n ih =>
    have himg : (Set.range fun Q : M => jv D (Sum.inr ((D.shM m)^[n + 1] Q)))
        = stepR D m '' Set.range fun Q : M => jv D (Sum.inr ((D.shM m)^[n] Q)) := by
      ext y
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨Q, rfl⟩
        refine ⟨_, ⟨Q, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
        show step D m (jv D (Sum.inr ((D.shM m)^[n] Q))) = jv D (Sum.inr ((D.shM m)^[n + 1] Q))
        rw [step_jv, Function.iterate_succ_apply']
        rfl
      · rintro ⟨_, ⟨Q, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
        refine ⟨Q, ?_⟩
        show jv D (Sum.inr ((D.shM m)^[n + 1] Q)) = step D m (jv D (Sum.inr ((D.shM m)^[n] Q)))
        rw [step_jv, Function.iterate_succ_apply']
        rfl
    rw [himg, closure_span_image_eq (stepR D m) (stepR_symm D m) ?_ ?_, ih]
    · intro x _ hx
      exact step_injective D m hx
    · rintro _ ⟨Q, rfl⟩
      rw [ih]
      show step D m (jv D (Sum.inr ((D.shM m)^[n] Q))) ∈ obsV D
      rw [step_jv]
      exact Submodule.le_topologicalClosure _ (Submodule.subset_span ⟨D.shM m ((D.shM m)^[n] Q), rfl⟩)

/-- **A smoothing operator for the joint data**: a real-linear continuous map on `JH D`, symmetric,
injective on `allV D`, carrying every joint vector into the observer's closed span. DERIVED: `0` the
zero vector. -/
def Smoothing : Prop :=
  ∃ A : JH D →L[ℝ] JH D, (∀ x y, RCLike.re (inner ℂ (A x) y) = RCLike.re (inner ℂ x (A y)))
    ∧ (∀ x ∈ allV D, A x = 0 → x = 0) ∧ ∀ x, A (jv D x) ∈ obsV D

/-- **Cyclicity from a smoothing operator** (`le_of_symm_injective`). DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem cyclic_of_smoothing (h : Smoothing D) : ObserverCyclic D := by
  letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ (JH D) := InnerProductSpace.complexToReal
  obtain ⟨A, hA, hinj, hAv⟩ := h
  show (Submodule.span ℝ (Set.range (jv D))).topologicalClosure ≤ obsV D
  refine le_of_symm_injective (isClosed_obsV D) (obsV_le_allV D) A hA hinj ?_
  rintro _ ⟨x, rfl⟩
  exact hAv x

/-- **Cyclicity from an operator with dense range on `allV`** carrying every joint vector into `obsV`
(`le_of_denseRange`; no symmetry). DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem cyclic_of_denseRange (A : JH D →L[ℝ] JH D)
    (hd : allV D ≤ ((allV D).map (A : JH D →ₗ[ℝ] JH D)).topologicalClosure)
    (hAv : ∀ x, A (jv D x) ∈ obsV D) : ObserverCyclic D := by
  show (Submodule.span ℝ (Set.range (jv D))).topologicalClosure ≤ obsV D
  refine le_of_denseRange (isClosed_obsV D) A hd ?_
  rintro _ ⟨x, rfl⟩
  exact hAv x

/-- **A smoothing operator exists iff the observer is cyclic** (`A = id` for the converse): the smoothing
form re-expresses `ObserverCyclic`, with the content in the identification of `A`. DERIVED: no
numeral. -/
theorem smoothing_iff_cyclic : Smoothing D ↔ ObserverCyclic D := by
  refine ⟨cyclic_of_smoothing D, fun h => ⟨ContinuousLinearMap.id ℝ (JH D), fun _ _ => rfl,
    fun _ _ hx => hx, fun x => h ?_⟩⟩
  exact Submodule.le_topologicalClosure _ (Submodule.subset_span ⟨x, rfl⟩)

end Joint

